0026 — an arc follows its world transform.

`emit_arc` drew in screen space from the node's own `arc-start` and
returned at once under any world that was not axis-aligned: a ring of arcs
on a rotating wrapper drew NOTHING while the wrapper was turned, so films
turned every arc by animating its `arcStart` instead. Now an axis-aligned
world with one scale on both axes keeps the screen-space path unchanged,
and every other world — rotation, a mirror, a skew, a scale that differs per
axis — goes through `emit_arc_transformed`: each 2x2 sample point is taken
back through the inverse of the world into the node's own frame and tested
against the arc there (ring, angle and caps in local pixels), with the
screen-space path's samples, coverage and RECT runs. So a rotation turns
the arc, a mirror runs its sweep the other way, and a scale that differs
per axis is the same ring stretched — an elliptical band whose stroke and
caps stretch with it. That last one is a change for an axis-aligned
`scale-x-*` on its own too, which used to draw a circle sized by the y
scale. Rows are clamped to where a sample can reach the outer circle and
skip where every sample is in the hole, both solved per row from the
inverse map, so a thin ring scans its band, not its disc.

Class `upstream`: the arc is the core's emission, drawn by every backend
as RECT runs; nothing target-side changes.

Guard: `an_arc_turns_mirrors_and_stretches_with_its_ancestors`
(`engine/core/src/tests.rs`): a quarter arc under a wrapper turned 30, 90,
135, 210 and -60 degrees has the ink angle and area of the unturned arc
with its start moved by the turn (within 1 degree and 2 %); under
`scaleX(-1)` it runs from 12 to 9 o'clock; a ring under `scaleX(2)` is
twice as wide as it is tall. Red before (the turned arc drew nothing),
green after.

Ledgers, against the same tree without this patch: `compositions/smoke`
moves, all 450 frames — its `arc-start-[220] arc-sweep-[280] arc-width-[10]
animate-spin` ring sits under a rotation on every frame and drew nothing on
any of them; it now draws and turns. No other digest and no `visibility` row
moves. `compositions/reel` prints smoke's earlier digest (`947ec6d2…`) as
text, quoting the dated measurement in `baselines/hash-portability.md`;
neither is a check, and neither is changed here.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

